<h3>2. Server log files</h3>
<p>
    The web server automatically stores technical logs when the site is accessed. This may include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>IP address (shortened or anonymised if configured)</li>
    <li>Date and time of request</li>
    <li>Accessed URL</li>
    <li>Referrer and browser information</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Processing is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR for technical operation and security. Logs are kept for a
    limited time and not used for profiling.
</p>

<h3>3. Stored search runs</h3>
<p>
    When you start a search, the task description you enter, any clarification answers, the
    intermediate results and the generated review are stored on the server. This storage is
    necessary to provide the service itself, including shareable result links (Art. 6(1)(b)
    GDPR). Run records are not linked to your name or account; do not include personal data in
    task descriptions.
</p>

<h3>4. AI processing by third parties</h3>
<p>
    To generate the review, the task description and intermediate results are transmitted to
    external large-language-model providers (via the OpenRouter API). These providers process
    the text to produce the response; depending on the provider, processing may take place
    outside the EU. No other data, in particular no IP address tied to the request content,
    is shared with them. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, as this processing is what the
    service consists of.
</p>

<h3>5. Cookies and analytics</h3>
<p>
    The site stores the access password locally in your browser so you do not have to re-enter
    it. No analytics or third-party tracking tools are used.
</p>

<h3>6. Contact by email</h3>
<p>
    If you send an email, your message and contact details are processed to handle your request. The legal
    basis is Art. 6(1)(b) or Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
</p>

<h3>7. Your rights</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Right of access</li>
    <li>Right to rectification</li>
    <li>Right to erasure</li>
    <li>Right to restriction of processing</li>
    <li>Right to data portability</li>
    <li>Right to object</li>
</ul>

